      "state": "open",
      "title": "security: replace GTK3/glib before 2026-10-31",
      "updated_at": "2026-09-30T07:34:38Z",
      "body": "## Scope\nReplace or remove the Linux GTK3 dependency path that currently resolves glib 0.18.x and triggers RUSTSEC-2024-0429 / Dependabot alert #1.\n\n## Current evidence\n- glib is transitive through gtk 0.18 / WebKitGTK and is only compiled on the Linux desktop path.\n- The formal Loom release is Windows-only; Linux publication is blocked until this issue is closed or freshly reassessed.\n- glib 0.20 cannot be introduced independently because the current GTK3 parent requires the 0.18 API line.\n- Temporary OSV exception expires 2026-10-31 and must not be renewed automatically.\n\n## Exit criteria\n1. Replace the GTK3/WebKitGTK parent with a compatible maintained stack, or remove the Linux target.\n2. Regenerate all Cargo.lock files through Cargo.\n3. Run the unconfigured and configured OSV scans plus Linux tests.\n4. Remove RUSTSEC-2024-0429 from security/osv-scanner.toml and close Dependabot alert #1."
    },
    "LoongPort399": "tracking issue, no compatible migration; contains no-direct-call reachability argument and disabled Dependabot security updates, neither adopted"
  },
